<title>CANADA: Russel Metals shuffles top executives.</title>
<headline>Russel Metals shuffles top executives.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russel Metals Inc said on Tuesday its chairman and chief executive, John Pelton, will replace Wayne Mang as company president following the annual shareholders meeting on May 14.</p>
<p>Russel said Mang, a director since 1993, will not stand for re-election.</p>
<p>It said Edward Siegel was appointed executive vice-president and chief operating officer of Russel's core metals business, effective immediately. Siegel has headed the company's international and specialty division for 10 years.</p>
<p>((Reuters Toronto Bureau (416) 941-8100))</p>
